devices lists every radio (SDR) the daemon has found, with its tuning range,
sample rates (how wide a band it can take in at once) and gain elements
(the amplifier stages 'ley set gain' adjusts). An empty list on a terminal
is followed by a checklist of what to try. --watch keeps running and prints
a line whenever a radio is plugged in or removed. Row numbers from this
list are accepted wherever a device id is (ley tune --device 2).

Usage:
  ley devices [flags]
  ley devices [command]

Examples:
  ley devices              # is my radio visible?
  ley devices --watch      # print a line on plug and unplug
  ley devices detach 2     # remove the second listed file playback device

Available Commands:
  detach      Remove a file playback device left behind by ley play

Flags:
  -h, --help    help for devices
      --watch   keep running and print a line when a radio is plugged in or removed

Global Flags:
      --json            machine output: proto3 JSON (NDJSON for streams)
      --socket string   daemon socket path (default: user daemon UDS, $LEYLINE_SOCKET)

Use "ley devices [command] --help" for more information about a command.
